  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "liquid drum and bass: the two-step with softly swung sixteenth hats and shaker, electric-piano seventh chords on the offbeats, a rolling sub",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "The two-step made smooth: the kick is the plain two-step, the snare carries fewer ghosts, the hats are sixteenths with a light swing and the shaker doubles them quietly. The chords are stacked sevenths struck on the one and pushed on the and of two, ringing, the way liquid producers voice a Rhodes. The sub rolls inside a fifth."
  }
